statement:
Let $f: \mathbb{N} \to \mathbb{N}$ be a function defined by $f(1) = 2$, $f(2) = 3$, and for all $n \in \mathbb{N}$,
$$f(f(f(n))) = \begin{cases} 
n + 2, & \text{if $n$ is even} \\
n + 4, & \text{if $n$ is odd}
\end{cases}$$
Prove that $f(777) = 390$.

