statement:
Prove that if \( x, y \in \left[-\frac{\pi}{6}, \frac{\pi}{6}\right] \) and \( a \in \mathbb{R} \) satisfy \(\left\{
\begin{array}{l}
x^{3} + \sin x - 3a = 0 \\
9y^{3} + \frac{1}{3} \sin 3y + a = 0
\end{array}
\right.\), then \( \cos (x + 3y)=1 \).

